the view dump stopped at depth 12 and said nothing

CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS walks the window and names every view and its frame. It stopped at depth 12 and
returned silently, which is worse than having no limit: iA Writer's tree is deeper than that, so a
dump taken specifically to find its table views did not contain them, and their absence read as
"there is no such view".

MEASURED: 116 lines of one dump sat at exactly the limit, and grepping the result for IATableView
or IAOutlineView returned nothing at all. With the limit raised they are both there with real
geometry, IATableView_Aspects_ 295x523 at 0,0 and IAOutlineView_Aspects_ 231x510, neither hidden.
That is what task #210 needed to know: the views exist and are correctly sized, so a click that
does nothing is not a missing or zero-sized view.

The limit is 32 now, it takes an override from the env var value (CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS=40), and when
it does stop it SAYS SO on a line of its own rather than just ending.

--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -220,8 +220,25 @@
  * and any string it can be asked for. CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS. */
 static void _CiderDumpViewTree(NSView *view, int depth)
 {
-    if (view == nil || depth > 12)
+    /* THE DEPTH LIMIT USED TO BE 12 AND SILENT, which is worse than no limit: iA Writer's tree is
+     * deeper than that, so its table views were absent from a dump taken to find them and the
+     * absence read as "no such view". Raised, and it now SAYS when it stops. Set the env var to a
+     * number to override, e.g. CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS=40. */
+    static int limit = 0;
+
+    if (limit == 0) {
+        const char *want = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS");
+        int parsed = (want != NULL) ? atoi(want) : 0;
+        limit = (parsed > 1) ? parsed : 32;
+    }
+
+    if (view == nil)
+        return;
+    if (depth > limit) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_VIEW %*sTRUNCATED at depth %d, raise CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS\n",
+                depth * 2, "", limit);
         return;
+    }
 
     NSRect frame = [view frame];
     NSString *text = nil;
